  "verifiedFindings": [
    "The named compulsory courses and one approved 6 EC elective produce 60+60+60 EC with no formal route. The course list confirms Payroll Taxes and Taxation and Technology and the separate 6 EC seminar and thesis.",
    "B6 accepts the first-year Dutch Financial Accounting 1 for Economics code 6011PN230 for both advanced accounting courses, settling the English-title hyperlinks in their shared catalogue entries. The earlier tax introductions satisfy the prerequisites for corporate income tax, VAT, international tax, director-shareholder taxation and taxable profit. Finance 1 precedes Finance 2.",
    "The Taxation and Government catalogue description explicitly includes second-year bachelor students. The embedded bare Essay minor reference is a label without a condition or qualifying instruction. B6 lists no entry requirement for this course. This supports retaining the required course in the normal degree sequence.",
    "The elective slot preserves a single 6 EC selection from the listed group. Business Analytics permits Economics and Business bachelor students outside the Business Analytics degree and asks for basic statistics and regression, covered by the first-year quantitative analysis course.",
    "The final-year graduation seminar follows completion of the first two years and 120 EC. European Tax Law is recommended preparation only for the seminar. The thesis follows the seminar."
  ],
  "essentialEvidence": "Confirm whether the faculty-specific entry rule in Fiscal Economics OER B6 is sufficient for regular bachelor access to 3313GEBRVY when the shared Law catalogue lists minor enrolment.",
  "officialAlternative": "UvA Economics and Business OER B6 Arts. 3.3–3.4, pp. 70–73, lists the compulsory 3 EC EU Tax course and gives two second-year tax prerequisites, both earlier in the degree. Its Part A Art. 4.1(4) refers students to Part B and the catalogue. The dated shared 3313GEBRVY entry expressly identifies minor enrolment and contains no separate bachelor rule. By contrast, the neighbouring International Tax entry expressly admits Fiscal Economics students. The degree’s elective guidance permits individual minor courses subject to their entry requirements. Its practical page confirms degree students register for themselves after year one and must heed course entry requirements. These official alternatives provide substantive evidence for the degree-specific progression but do not explicitly reconcile the conflicting enrolment condition.",
  "nextAction": "Resume CP397 with source attempt two. Seek the 2026–2027 faculty erratum, course-specific bachelor placement rule, or documented faculty precedence for 3313GEBRVY. Keep the verified 177 EC, all interest rows and three feasible provisional UCR trials. Reassess full comparability and complete final checks once the entry rule is resolved."
}
